    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the early 1890s, Menifee was highlighted as a model African‑American community in an 1896 Freeman newspaper article.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofmenifeear.org/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Menifee’s growth in Howard Township from 1870 to 1890 was driven by black families migrating from the east and cotton sharecropping opportunities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofmenifeear.org/our-history",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Menifee officially incorporated as a city during the 1960s after recognizing the need for qualified municipal status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofmenifeear.org/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Menifee’s local economy relies heavily on lumber and wood products, employing 200–250 people across eight facilities.",
